  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to replant; to transplant; to repot",
      "explanation": "To move a plant from one location or container to another. Common in gardening contexts."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "17856_uekaeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{花|はな}を{大|おお}きい{鉢|はち}に{植|う}え{替|か}えた。",
      "english": "I replanted the flower in a bigger pot.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "17856_uekaeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{春|はる}になったら{苗|なえ}を{庭|にわ}に{植|う}え{替|か}える{予定|よてい}だ。",
      "english": "I plan to transplant the seedlings to the garden in spring.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "17856_uekaeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{根|ね}が{詰|つ}まってきたので、そろそろ{植|う}え{替|か}えた{方|ほう}がいい。",
      "english": "The roots are getting crowded, so you should repot it soon.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\nPrimarily a gardening term. The noun form {植|う}え{替|か}え refers to the act of replanting/repotting. Spring is the most common time for {植|う}え{替|か}え in Japan.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {鉢|はち}に{植|う}え{替|か}える (to repot)\n- {庭|にわ}に{植|う}え{替|か}える (to transplant into the garden)\n- {植|う}え{替|か}えの{時期|じき} (repotting season)\n- {苗|なえ}を{植|う}え{替|か}える (to transplant seedlings)",
